<title>FRANCE: Club Med's Trigano quits in &quot;Mickey&quot; jibe.</title>
<headline>Club Med's Trigano quits in &quot;Mickey&quot; jibe.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The ex-chairman of holiday firm Club Mediterranee, Serge Trigano, said on Friday he was resigning from the company's supervisory board in a row over style with the company's new chairman, former Euro Disney boss Philippe Bourguignon.</p>
<p>Trigano, son of Club Med's co-founder Gilbert Trigano, told French radio on the day the firm unveiled a 413 million franc first-half loss that its famous resorts risked turning into &quot;Mickey (Mouse) clubs&quot; and it was time for the founders to quit.</p>
</text>
